-- title:
--   Constant and multiplicative rank-q Hopf algebra models
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a nontrivial commutative ring, let $q$ be a natural number with $q \neq 0$, and let $L$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero equipped with an $R$-algebra structure. The conclusion is a conjunction of two existence statements, each asserting the existence of a type $K$ carrying a commutative ring structure and an $R$-Hopf algebra structure such that $K$ is finite as an $R$-module, flat as an $R$-module, has $\operatorname{finrank}_R K = q$, and the set of $R$-algebra homomorphisms $K \to L$ has cardinality exactly $q$ (as a `Nat.card`). The two statements differ in the prescribed shape of the underlying $R$-algebra: in the first, $K$ is $R$-algebra isomorphic to the product algebra $\mathrm{Fin}\,q \to R$, i.e. to $R^{q}$ with componentwise operations; in the second, $K$ is $R$-algebra isomorphic to $R[X]/(X^{q}-1)$, the quotient of the polynomial ring by the ideal generated by $X^{q}-1$. Note that the Hopf algebra structures are existentially quantified, so no particular comultiplication is named in the statement.
--
--   These are the coordinate rings of the constant group scheme $\underline{\mathbb{Z}/q}_R$ and of the group scheme $\mu_{q,R}$ of $q$-th roots of unity, exhibited here as finite flat commutative Hopf algebras of rank $q$ over an arbitrary nontrivial base, each with exactly $q$ points valued in an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero. The result supplies the standard rank-$q$ models used in the analysis of finite flat group schemes attached to torsion in the Néron model of $J_0(N)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HopfAlgebra_exists_constant_and_rootsOfUnity_models_of_rank.lean

